From f5d98a4c64d0e37c51aa0f5d804cd699e941f14d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:02:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ai): show key rejected after a provider authentication
 failure

The provider Test control classifies an authentication failure before the
generic status match. HTTP 401 and 403 are key rejected, and a plain 400
is key rejected only with the provider-documented auth error field
(Anthropic authentication_error, OpenAI invalid_api_key, Gemini
API_KEY_INVALID, UNAUTHENTICATED or the API-key-not-valid message). The
status line reads "Test failed: the key was rejected". The key stays
removed and the provider response is not shown. A wrong model, missing
credit, a rate limit, an outage and a network error keep their own
statuses. Tests pin each provider and the distinct causes.

Fixes #3804
